cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Code for: Small-Scale Corrections to the Kirchhoff Approximation for Scattering from Multi-Scale Rough Dielectric Surfaces"
abstract: >-
  Python code that generates the figures of the Results section and the validation scripts of the paper. The Kirchhoff approximation
  (an expansion in the curvature of the surface) and the method of variation of boundaries (an expansion in its height) are combined for
  dielectric surfaces made of a smooth periodic profile carrying a small-scale roughness (1D, TE and TM). The boundary variations are taken
  about the periodic surface; the zeroth order is either the Kirchhoff amplitudes or the exact solution of the smooth profile. The reference
  solutions are an independent C-method solver and the Rayleigh method.
